Cell["\<\
referenceBands uses the {{kx,ky,kz},{energy1,energy2,...}} format returned by \
vaspEig. kRange is a nonempty list of 1-based record indices, and every \
selected record must contain exactly Dimensions[H][[1]] energies.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"554d2c2b-7c41-461d-9072-dfb9acba418b"],

Cell["\<\
The EnergyWindow, KPointNeighborhood, BandSelection, and ResidualWeights \
selectors are intersected with kRange. EnergyWindow masks individual \
reference energies, not complete k-point records.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4154a2f0-7c2c-498e-b67f-f21dc19ad4b2"],

Cell["\<\
KPointNeighborhood uses fractional reciprocal coordinates. With Periodic -> \
True, the displacement is reduced by the componentwise minimum-image \
convention before applying a spherical Radius or componentwise Range.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6d6e1363-aaff-4265-9159-ce744b51f873"],

Cell["\<\
BandSelection uses 1-based reference positions. At every retained k point, \
sorted model eigenvalue j is paired with reference position j; the reference \
bands are not dynamically reordered.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1399c8b9-2eaf-4da8-beda-7851e89c6759"],

Cell["\<\
ResidualWeights is Automatic or a nonnegative record-by-band matrix with the \
same shape as referenceBands[[All,2]]. A zero weight removes that residual; \
positive weights minimize the weighted sum of squared band differences.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9a89379c-b898-4527-9cc9-7791cc7fd347"],

Cell["\<\
initialRules can be a rule list or Association and must assign a real numeric \
starting value to every fitting parameter. H is evaluated at 2 Pi times each \
reciprocal-fractional k point.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"01d0cb2c-3cce-407f-b47d-d645787233cb"],

Cell["\<\
The Hamiltonian must be affine-linear in the fitting parameters. MagneticTB \
caches its constant and parameter-coefficient matrices, then uses a \
finite-difference Levenberg-Marquardt optimizer; it does not switch to a \
slower nonlinear symbolic fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0525bcde-66ed-408b-b120-99cd26c9e99b"],

Cell["\<\
The objective minimizes sorted energy residuals only. It does not preserve a \
band gap, band character, or a chosen band ordering; always inspect \
ComparisonPlot and reject a lower-loss fit when its band structure is \
physically wrong.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d6965cc9-f2db-451e-8b62-e62cda4da957"],

Cell["\<\
The result reports FittedParams, convergence diagnostics, ComparisonPlot, \
CandidateKPointCount, UsedKPointCount, UsedKPointIndices, ResidualCount, the \
effective selectors, weighting, and band pairing.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d41b7d7f-e2c6-49fd-b4ec-f9ae0c599b39"],

Cell["\<\
fittingTB returns $Failed and issues a message when the Hamiltonian or \
reference records are invalid, kRange or a selector is invalid, the combined \
selection is empty or underdetermined, initial values are incomplete, the \
model is nonlinear in its parameters, the time limit is exceeded, or the \
optimizer fails. It does not repair the input or switch to an approximate \
fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c3473c8a-d997-4b6a-843f-988db0621e2c"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "3f942a0f-1cfc-4ff1-bf95-9194d12b2d88"], "MaxIterations", "100", Cell["\<\
Positive integer upper bound on Levenberg-Marquardt iterations.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c2936ec1-067a-4250-bb86-043babfb4622"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "1110eae3-128a-4697-934a-96c2a39b90d3"], "TimeConstraint", "60", Cell[
    "Positive fitting time limit in seconds, or Infinity.", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"ac5633ca-7c7a-4e55-9a70-748c713a38dc"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "c5f821d0-4c3c-4e6a-b383-e2b51bbec9b5"], "\"\<EnergyWindow\>\"", "All", 
    Cell["\<\
All keeps every reference energy; {emin,emax} keeps energies in the inclusive \
interval.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a415ed62-1515-45f3-b7fd-5b67345fc4e8"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "6c267ff9-446a-4cca-bce7-98f947040e51"], "\"\<KPointNeighborhood\>\"", 
    "All", Cell["\<\
All keeps every k point; an Association selects a periodic or nonperiodic \
Radius or componentwise Range around Center.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c5d4311e-d064-4c36-a31d-5b34e33be67d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "b5b9c066-f238-4d6a-aef5-40af1a19e1a7"], "\"\<BandSelection\>\"", "All", 
    Cell["\<\
All keeps every reference position; an integer, increasing integer list, or \
positive-step Span selects 1-based band positions.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8aa120ff-70b1-4b8d-9955-07ee32d9972d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "c38484e2-8371-4aa1-af69-7a83f3d8872a"], "\"\<ResidualWeights\>\"", 
    "Automatic", Cell["\<\
Automatic assigns unit weight; a nonnegative record-by-band matrix weights \
individual residuals, with zero removing a residual.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"fe5d92fd-816d-42a9-99c5-2dc536e9827d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "9ff6fd57-bd35-4bf4-a48b-40a8d725feff"], "\"\<FiniteDifferenceStep\>\"", 
    
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}]}], Cell["\<\
Positive relative step used for central finite-difference Jacobian columns.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"34a7476d-d9a5-4f28-b0f9-32c73c6c629e"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "89dcfe07-dbc8-4b48-ac7e-7e4b089bb218"], "\"\<InitialDamping\>\"", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}]}], Cell[
    "Positive initial Levenberg-Marquardt damping factor.", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"2535d66d-fad5-47dd-a334-4d0eeb9721b4"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "47518385-53cb-4e95-b08c-aafd013fb5a3"], "\"\<FitTolerance\>\"", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}]}], Cell["\<\
Positive stopping tolerance for the gradient, step size, and objective \
improvement.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"603bb2b0-b83a-48c5-a167-58e0cf59cc16"]}
